 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 543351,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find a minimum spanning tree for the weighted graph. Give its total weight.\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Weighted Graph</figcaption>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/835a2f793b1983ff.png\" alt=\"A weighted graph with five vertices. The vertices are as follows: U, V, W, X, and Z. The edges are labeled as follows. U V, 89. V Y, 24. Y X, 68. X W, 45. W U, 37. U X, 49. W V, 68.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Rank the weights: 24, 37, 45, 49, 68, 68, 89</p>\n<p>Step 1: Choose the edge with the minimum weight of all the edges.</p>\n<p>VY has a weight of 24.</p>\n<p>Step 2: Choose another edge of minimum weight from the remaining edges. The second edge does not have to be connected to the first edge.</p>\n<p>UW has a weight of 37.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Choose another edge of minimum weight from the remaining edges, but do not select any edge that creates a cycle in the subgraph you are creating.</p>\n<p>WX has a weight of 45.</p>\n<p>Step 4: Repeat Step 3 until all the vertices of the original graph are included and you have a spanning tree.</p>\n<p>UX has a weight of 48. UX would create a cycle, so do not use it.</p>\n<p>Repeat Step 3: Choose another edge of minimum weight from the remaining edges, but do not select any edge that creates a cycle in the subgraph you are creating.</p>\n<p>There are two edges with a weight of 68. You can put either in your graph. VW or YX (not both)</p>\n<p>You are done. You now have five vertices in your graph.</p>\n<p>Add the weights: <span data-math=\"{\\text{24  +  37  +  45  +  68  = 174}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The weight of your spanning tree is 174.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "There are two possible minimum spanning trees, each with a total weight of 174:\n<br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBc1lMIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--62384ffbcf891a52a422e8f29a95a20403a7b8de/CS_Figure_12_10_280.png\" alt=\"Two weighted graphs. The vertices in each graph are as follows: U, V, W, X, and Y. The edges in the first graph are as follows. U W, 37. W X, 45. W V, 68. V Y, 24. The edges in the second graph are as follows. U W, 37. W X, 45. X Y, 68. Y V, 24.\">"
    }
   ],
